  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n- `post::dialect::declared_turning(cps) -> Result<Option<bool>, PostError>`: `Some(true/false)` for a declared `capabilities` mask, `None` when the script states no usable mask (absent, a string, negative, non-finite). `speaks_turning` keeps its meaning and is now `declared_turning(..)?.unwrap_or(false)`.\n- `app::lathe_voice::at_post` (the #1190 door) reads the tri-state: a declared turning script fires the door as before; a declared non-turning script passes as before; an **undeclared** script is held to the door for every operation whose setup mounts a machine with a work spindle (lathe or mill-turn, via `machine::kind_of_setup`), and the refusal adds that the script has no `capabilities` line and what to add (`capabilities = 1;` mill, `= 2;` turning). On a mill, plasma table or EDM (no work spindle) an undeclared script passes as before.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1199-undeclared-dialect.md`: option (b) of the issue; (a) refuse-everywhere and (c) warn-only considered and dropped, with reasons.\n\nBehaviour change for users: a user's own *milling* script without `capabilities`, posting a milling op on a lathe or mill-turn setup, is now refused by name with the one-line fix. Every shipped post states its mask, so no shipped post, golden or registry pairing changes.\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests:\n- `camcraft-app` lib `lathe_voice::tests::an_undeclared_script_is_held_to_the_door_on_a_machine_with_a_work_spindle`: an inline undeclared lathe script (also `capabilities = \"2\"` and `-1`) on a lathe and on a mill-turn refuses a Face op and an off-centre Drill by name (names the missing line, the machine, the fix), still passes Facing / on-centre Drill / C-stating live tool; declared `1` / `2` on the same machines behave as before; on a mill and with no machine loaded it passes. Fails on main (the door returned Ok).\n- `camcraft-post` lib `post::dialect::tests::an_undeclared_mask_is_none_never_a_guess`.\n- Unchanged and green: `lathe_voice::tests::the_door_refuses_on_every_turning_dialect_and_passes_every_milling_one` (every shipped post, every kind) and the other lathe_voice unit tests.\n\nSuites run (debug, all green): camcraft-app `posting`, `conformance`, `golden_cl`, `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_css`, `lathe_post_g76`, `lathe_post_refusals`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread`, `lathe_work_spindle`, `lathe_workholding_rpm`, `lathe_spindle_law`, `lathe_cross_drill`, `control_comp`, `drill_prior`, `per_op_files`, `setup_mount`, `setup_mounts_post`, `wear_comp`, `edm_machine`; the whole `camcraft-post` crate; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The GUI/MCP post entry points end-to-end with a user `.cps` file on disk (they all call `at_post`, covered at the door).\n- The rest of the app suites (batch tier).\n\nChangelog: A post script that does not state `capabilities` is now held to the lathe door on a lathe or mill-turn setup and refused by name for a milling operation, instead of being read as a mill post (#1199)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1199\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
